{"body":"The workspace verbs, the pre-merge steps and the primary-checkout rule asked the git binary for facts that sit in files. They now go through internal/git's client, one per worktree for the life of the process, which reads HEAD, the branch, the worktree list, refs, a remote's URL and the trunk from the repository's files and spawns git only for what it cannot read.\n\nversion: minor\n\n## What changed\n\n- `internal/git`: the client gains an inherit mode (for verbs the operator runs), `Do`/`Combined` with a per-call deadline and writers, `ResolveRef`, `Rev` and `RemoteURL`. `internal/run` counts the children it starts by program (`run.Started`), so a test can hold a verb to a number of git spawns.\n- `internal/workspace`: every `lightGit`/`gitNetwork*` call goes through the client (`gitclient.go`); plan steps that run git go through it too. A directory in no repository still runs the binary there, so git's own words come back.\n- `internal/tdd/merge`: the trunk, the checked-out branch, the origin URL and the worktree list are read from files (`gitfacts.go`).\n- No branch name is assumed. The default branch is the client's trunk; a verb that needs one and cannot tell refuses with `git remote set-head origin --auto` / `--base` instead of taking \"main\". The primary-checkout rule and `gate doctor` hold the checkout to the repo's trunk (`primaryBranch = \"main\"` is gone). `cli_workspace*` made no git calls of its own.\n- Staged-set cache key (`stagedmemo.go`) includes the commits trunk names during a merge, with a test where trunk moves to hold the incoming tip and the index, HEAD and MERGE_HEAD do not.\n- Three surviving mutants each get a test: `looksBare` (client.go), `firstToken` (refs.go), and the `otherWorktreeRoots` condition (failfirst_pytest_siblings.go), the latter proven by flipping the three parts of the condition by hand.\n- `workspace merge` and `--wait` say \"no check ran (all N skipped)\" when every check on the head concluded skipped. The verdict the gate may reuse already counted only `success`; a test pins that.\n\n## Git spawns per verb\n\nCounted by `run.Started(\"git\")` over a real repository with a bare origin (`gitspawns_test.go`):\n\n| verb | before | after |\n|---|---|---|\n| `workspace commit` | 8 | 5 |\n| `workspace merge` | 9 | 5 |\n\nThe merge's fifth is the sync step that records dropped queued PRs (#1202), which landed after the count was first taken at four.\n\n## Notes\n\n- The host port (F21b) follows as a second PR stacked on this one.\n- Mutation findings on the new lines are reported, not refused, in this repo; the commit gate's measurement ran out of its wall-clock budget on the larger commit and listed the rest as not measured.\n\nCloses #1191\n","title":"Read git facts from the repository files in the workspace and merge verbs"}
